  "qualifications": [
    "Same four reviewed August request cases and unchanged production reader SQL; first means a newly prepared statement on one fresh session, not cold disk or cold OS caches.",
    "The full PostgreSQL server restarted for deployment before this probe, but parent first-page HTTP validation preceded it. This measurement does not independently claim cold shared buffers.",
    "Each case includes a first EXPLAIN, three repeated fetches and a warm EXPLAIN. Instrumented whole-reader latency is not ordinary HTTP latency; the preserved topic whole-call time exceeded1second.",
    "First node/topic/topic-search execution remained slower than repeated execution. First planning also retains measurable metadata traversal cost; no identical-speed or constant-memory claim is made.",
    "Planner memory units are KiB from PostgreSQL Memory Used/Allocated, not process RSS. work_mem does not bound this planner context.",
    "Three warm fetches per case are descriptive, not a p95 sample. Separate HTTP/concurrent testing supplies operational acceptance.",
    "Generic-plan caching is per connection/statement and invalidations require rebuilding. Concurrent fresh-plan memory was not measured by this single-session probe.",
    "JIT was off in both before/after probes. The native patch preserves cost formulas; the separate289-case paired isolated gate verified exact rendered plans/costs and results."
